WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.300
-We're back with
Jennifer Hudson.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.133
You know, every time
you've been on the show,

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.601
we have talked about
your accomplishments,

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.267
but you had a really big one
since last time you're here.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.834
You were a producer
on a Broadway show.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.400
-Yes.
-"A Strange Loop."

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.467
-"A Strange Loop."
-Won a Tony.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.767
That was your Tony
that completed an EGOT.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:20.167
You've got all four --
Emmy, Grammy, Oscar, Tony.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.767
-Yeah, that was surreal.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.767
You know, I went
in support of the cast.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.067
-Yeah.
-And when they said

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.601
"Strange Loop" won
for Best Musical,

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.834
I'm up there cheering
for the cast,

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:32.567
and everyone started chanting,
"EGOT, EGOT."

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.567
and I'm like, oh, whoa.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.300
I just won an EGOT.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.834
-Yeah.
-They say that EGOT's

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.834
most likely to happen when you
don't know it's happened.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.100
-[ Laughs ] I guess so.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.934
-It's like a watched tea kettle
never whatever --

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.834
You know what I mean?
They say that about EGOTs.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:54.834
So did you -- now you've got --
How do you display them?

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:58.067
-Well, I have an award wall
in my home in Chicago,

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.367
and the Oscar
sits in the middle.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.100
And it says, "Haaaa!"

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.901
And I said I would never
reveal the award wall

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.267
until the EGOT was complete.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.601
But now that it is,
I think I need to,

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:14.100
like, redo the award wall,
and then I'll reveal it.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.000
-I think you should have, like,
a mechanical sliding wall.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.434
And when people come in,
they just see the Emmy,

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:20.767
and you're like,
yeah, I just won an Emmy.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:23.467
And then you hit a button
and it's like,

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:26.133
oh, that's right,
I also have a Grammy.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.834
Well, I'm sure
that's all of it.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.067
[ Both imitating door opening ]

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.501
-I like that.
-Yeah. That's fun, right?

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.968
-You gon' wake up
and I'm gon' have it now, okay?

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:36.868
-I have good ideas about it

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:39.367
because I'm never going to
win the awards.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.901
So you know what? I will give it
to you as a gift. Yeah.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.000
-Okay. All right.
I will hold on to that.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.334
-Do you have any dream guests?
Throw it out in the universe

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.601
for the next time you're here.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:50.801
Who would you like to have on?

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:55.033
-Of course, Taylor Swift.
I would love to have her.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:58.033
Um, Michael Jordan
is a dream of mine.

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:01.234
I know, I know
that's a tough dream.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:04.033
And if I could pick Zendaya.
-Oh, that's a good three.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.234
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's a good three.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.834
Well, I wish that
you get all of that.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.968
I feel like
with everything you have,

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.934
I can't imagine you're not
going to get that as well.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.634
-Okay.
-And now you were talking

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.467
about your son, and how many --

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.834
how often does
he come and see your show?

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:21.434
-Not often, because
he's a basketball kid.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.400
So he's heavily into sports.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.767
-Okay.
How old is he now?

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.133
-He's 14.
-Oh, yeah. There you go.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:28.701
-Yes. And now he's going
to school out in LA.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.200
-Okay.
-So that's a new thing.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.501
Before, I could drop him off at
school and then go to work.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.300
-That's very exciting.
-Yes, it's very exciting.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.334
-So you do need to have like
a basketball guest on the show

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:37.634
to have him show
any interest at all?

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:40.267
-I mean, then I'll be cool.
-Yeah?

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.801
It breaks my heart that
you're not cool to your son.

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:45.267
-You know? To your kids,
you're just Mom.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.734
-Yeah. That's true.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.300
-No matter how many people --
like,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.868
when I walk my kids to school,
every now and then,

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.000
people will be like,
"Hey, I love your show."

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.267
And they're like,
"Oh, what's that about?"

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.033
I'm like, "I have a show."
They're like, "When?"

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.400
-See?
-Yeah.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.868
-Exactly. So you understand.
-Yeah. It's heartbreaking.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.400
You know what my son said to me
the other day?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.934
"When you die,
do I get your show?"

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:08.167
-David, don't you say that
to me. [ Laughs ]

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:09.834
Mine told me,
"Don't embarrass me."

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.534
-Oh, yeah. That's fair.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:12.868
That's fair
not to be embarrassed.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.667
Mine aren't old enough
to know what shame is yet.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.400
-Well, you just wait.
-I know.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.801
You know what we do
every year?

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.467
And we'll do it -- We're going
to film it this week.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:22.367
So every Thanksgiving
since my son was --

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.300
I guess he was six months old

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.701
when we did our
Thanksgiving show.

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.834
We dressed him up as a turkey --
like as a baby in a turkey suit.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.167
And then we've been
adding each year,

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.100
and now I got three kids
that we're dressing up

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.567
in a turkey suit.
And one of these days,

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.501
one of his friends at school
is going to be like,

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:40.033
"I saw you dressed
like a [bleep] turkey."

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.434
And he's going to come home
and be like,

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.534
"I did not consent to this."

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:44.901
-See?
-That day is going to come.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.267
-See?
-That day is gonna come.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:49.901
-Get ready.
-Yeah. Well, whatever.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:51.334
Look, he should be happy.
When I die,

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.734
all of this is his.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.234
-That is true.
-That is true.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.234
-That is true.
-Did you have any --

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.901
you know, like, when
I got this show, you know,

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:02.234
I obviously had in mind
the people who had it before,

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:03.634
you know, from Letterman
to Conan to Jimmy.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:04.901
Like, what were
the daytime shows

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:07.000
that you were most impressed by?

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.300
-Well, of course, Oprah,

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.200
I loved -- I grew up
watching Oprah's show.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.667
I love "The Ellen Show" as well.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:16.200
And then I'm into like,
Tamron and Sherri

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.501
now as well, too.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:18.801
-That's really cool.
It's really cool

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:21.067
to have those people
that were trailblazers that have

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.968
this path made for you.
It's really wonderful to watch.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.467
-Yeah, I get
to learn from them all.

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.634
-There you go.
-And have my host voice.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.033
-Yeah, you're very good.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.100
Thank you for
making it back here.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.634
And congratulations
on everything.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:31.734
-Thank you for having me.
-You guys,

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.634
that's Jennifer Hudson.

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:35.934
"The Jennifer Hudson Show"
airs weekdays.

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:36.968
Check your local listings

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.467
and stick around
for Matt Rogers.

